# 5. Windows Update Troubleshooting

When a user reports that Windows Update is failing, I should not immediately make major system changes.

### Basic Troubleshooting

1. Ask when the problem started.
2. Ask whether any recent changes were made.
3. Record the error message or error code.
4. Check network connectivity.
5. Check available disk space.
6. Check Windows Update-related services.
7. Review relevant Event Viewer logs.
8. Retry the update according to company procedure.
9. Verify the result.
10. Document the troubleshooting steps.
11. Escalate if necessary.

