# 6. Active Directory User Management

Active Directory Users and Computers (ADUC) can be used to create and manage domain user accounts and group memberships when the administrator has the appropriate permissions.

## 6.1 Creating a User

Basic workflow:

```text
Active Directory Users and Computers
        ↓
Select appropriate OU
        ↓
New
        ↓
User
        ↓
Enter user information
        ↓
Set password
        ↓
Apply company password policy
        ↓
Create account
```

A temporary password can be assigned and the user can be required to change it at their next logon, depending on organizational policy.

---

# 7. Active Directory Group Membership

Security groups allow administrators to organize accounts into manageable units and commonly provide access to resources through group membership.

### Basic Workflow

```text
User
 ↓
Properties
 ↓
Member Of
 ↓
Add
 ↓
Select Security Group
 ↓
Apply
```

### Why use Security Groups?

Instead of assigning permissions individually to every user, permissions can be assigned to a group and users can receive access through their group membership.

### Example

```text
Finance Security Group
        ↓
Finance Shared Folder Permission
        ↓
Finance Users
```

This improves consistency and reduces administrative effort.

