# 9. Locked vs Disabled Accounts

## Locked Account

A locked account is temporarily prevented from authenticating, commonly because the account-lockout policy was triggered after repeated failed authentication attempts.

### Help Desk workflow

```text
Verify user identity
        ↓
Check account status
        ↓
Unlock account if authorized
        ↓
Verify login
        ↓
Document
```

If the account becomes locked again, investigate the underlying cause rather than repeatedly unlocking it.

---

## Disabled Account

A disabled account still exists in Active Directory but is prevented from new sign-ins.

An administrator can disable or enable the account through ADUC.

### Important distinction

```text
Locked
↓
Authentication temporarily blocked

Disabled
↓
Account intentionally disabled

Deleted
↓
Account removed from Active Directory
```

