# 19. Behavioral Interview Practice

### Question

**How do you troubleshoot an issue when you don't know the cause?**

### Professional Answer

> I start by gathering information from the user and understanding when the issue started, whether any changes were made, and whether other users are affected. Based on the information I collect, I identify the most likely causes and test the simplest and safest possibilities first. I make changes only when I understand the potential impact and have the appropriate authorization. After making a change, I verify the result with the user. Finally, I document the troubleshooting steps and resolution, or escalate the issue if it requires additional access or expertise.

